  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A short bar magnet is placed in the magnetic meridian of the earth with North Pole pointing north. Neutral points are found at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;from the magnet on the East-West line, drawn through the middle point of the magnet. The magnetic moment of the magnet in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Am</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is close to:<br /><br />(Given <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math> in SI units and <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math> Horizontal component of earth&#39;s magnetic field <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> Tesla.)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
